(4541548, 650540, 67018, '<td valign="top">Something really needs to be done with obviously jealous inept supposed "photographers" giving ridiculous low scores for images like this. <br/> <br/>Seems it happens every contest and sometimes can make the difference between places or even getting a ribbon. <br/> <br/>The odd low scores should be thrown out. <br/> <br/>Gene<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-05 18:28:27.</i></td>', 'Something really needs to be done with obviously jealous inept supposed "photographers" giving ridiculous low scores for images like this.  Seems it happens every contest and sometimes can make the difference between places or even getting a ribbon.  The odd low scores should be thrown out.  Gene', '2008-03-05 18:27:47.000000', '2008-03-05 18:28:27.000000', 0),
(4541642, 650540, 67723, '<td valign="top">pretty sweet!</td>', 'pretty sweet!', '2008-03-05 19:11:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4541643, 651131, 67723, '<td valign="top">This is like the best photo EVER!!!  Congrats Jessy</td>', 'This is like the best photo EVER!!!  Congrats Jessy', '2008-03-05 19:12:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4541695, 651728, 67723, '<td valign="top">wow you have gotten so many top 10''s lately!  way to go...</td>', 'wow you have gotten so many top 10''s lately!  way to go...', '2008-03-05 19:27:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4541953, 651599, 5286, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kavey:</b></div><hr/><i> In my opinion, this is the best in the challenge. I think it''s perfect as it is, not too cluttered, the wine bottle and glass are very obvious even with such shallow DOF, the composition is perfect, the lighting colour and strength is perfect...<br/>Can you let us in on some of your processing? Is some of the OOF blur added in processing? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No blurring in PP; it was just shot at f1.8, the wine glass and bottle are pretty far away relative to the cherries. There wasn''t too much PP, main thing was dogding around the cherries a little to highlight them.</td>', 'Originally posted by Kavey: In my opinion, this is the best in the challenge. I think it''s perfect as it is, not too cluttered, the wine bottle and glass are very obvious even with such shallow DOF, the composition is perfect, the lighting colour and strength is perfect...Can you let us in on some of your processing? Is some of the OOF blur added in processing?  No blurring in PP; it was just shot at f1.8, the wine glass and bottle are pretty far away relative to the cherries. There wasn''t too much PP, main thing was dogding around the cherries a little to highlight them.', '2008-03-05 21:25:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542054, 650540, 4793, '<td valign="top">Beautiful</td>', 'Beautiful', '2008-03-05 22:06:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542062, 650540, 7467, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your win - this is a great shot. I read your comments with interest, about people "purposfully" voting low - on an obviously great picture. I had a couple of 1''s on my shot also (5th place Swans). Is this a regular thing?<br/>Drake</td>', 'Congrats on your win - this is a great shot. I read your comments with interest, about people "purposfully" voting low - on an obviously great picture. I had a couple of 1''s on my shot also (5th place Swans). Is this a regular thing?Drake', '2008-03-05 22:11:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542094, 651131, 25355, '<td valign="top">Textures and colour are perfect, and the good old Rule of Thirds. ;-) Congratulations.</td>', 'Textures and colour are perfect, and the good old Rule of Thirds. ;-) Congratulations.', '2008-03-05 22:30:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542112, 650540, 42567, '<td valign="top">OMGosh, it was me who gave you a 1  !!!   I think I''ll try this easy shot next time I need a blue!! wooohooo!!!!!!!!<br/> Blah<br/> <br/></td>', 'OMGosh, it was me who gave you a 1  !!!   I think I''ll try this easy shot next time I need a blue!! wooohooo!!!!!!!! Blah ', '2008-03-05 22:38:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542215, 649644, 1041, '<td valign="top">Very creative and beautiful</td>', 'Very creative and beautiful', '2008-03-05 23:14:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542224, 650882, 34114, '<td valign="top">Yum....sorry it didn''t score higher for you, Enzo.</td>', 'Yum....sorry it didn''t score higher for you, Enzo.', '2008-03-05 23:22:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542349, 650371, 19936, '<td valign="top">What are you having a heat wave down there!  No ladybugs for me yet.<br/> <br/>Anyway, great job and, ho hum, another ribbon.</td>', 'What are you having a heat wave down there!  No ladybugs for me yet. Anyway, great job and, ho hum, another ribbon.', '2008-03-06 00:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542352, 650540, 19936, '<td valign="top">Great shot even if it is an overdone subject.  Someone is going to have to take that macro away from you.  Not to mention the creative ideas!</td>', 'Great shot even if it is an overdone subject.  Someone is going to have to take that macro away from you.  Not to mention the creative ideas!', '2008-03-06 00:32:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542355, 651131, 19936, '<td valign="top">Wow! I was wondering if this would do this well.  I thought it might get hurt by the narrow DOF.  It works for me because of the great blend.  Good job and congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Wow! I was wondering if this would do this well.  I thought it might get hurt by the narrow DOF.  It works for me because of the great blend.  Good job and congrats on the ribbon.', '2008-03-06 00:35:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542365, 650048, 68035, '<td valign="top">Wow...I cant believe how well you capture the fur, you have textured it so that I can almost feel its softness.<br/> <br/>The other thing that stands out for me are the facing lions eyelids as I dont think I have ever seen these in such detail and I am genuinely fascinated by them<br/> <br/>As ever a wonderful animal shot that stops the viewer dead in their tracks when it opens on screen<br/></td>', 'Wow...I cant believe how well you capture the fur, you have textured it so that I can almost feel its softness. The other thing that stands out for me are the facing lions eyelids as I dont think I have ever seen these in such detail and I am genuinely fascinated by them As ever a wonderful animal shot that stops the viewer dead in their tracks when it opens on screen', '2008-03-06 00:52:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542497, 650599, 42902, '<td valign="top">thanks for all the constructive comments, however i would like to point out that this is a color on color photo even if on some monitors it might not look so.<br/>the background is clearly dark red and i take no blame for the constructor''s decision to put a big yellow logo on that beautiful red car, but that shouldn''t have been a problem since the photo that placed in front of me had a bunch of strawberrys with a lot of green on a reddish background (and even the winner has a lot of white on that lemon, but then white is not really a color right? :P).<br/> <br/>all in all, seeing the comments i realize that i may have messed with the contrast a bit too much but, in my opinion, the best way to outline a Ferrari is to present it on a dark background (and the challenge rules didn''t say anything about the luminosity of the background or that of the subject, just that they should be of the same color). And, it''s true, I oversharpend it just a bit to enhance the lines even more.<br/> <br/>i was expecting more comments on the photo itself than on the challenge requirements, anyway i placed a request for a review from the club, if they''ll ever get to my photo...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-06 16:08:06.</i></td>', 'thanks for all the constructive comments, however i would like to point out that this is a color on color photo even if on some monitors it might not look so.the background is clearly dark red and i take no blame for the constructor''s decision to put a big yellow logo on that beautiful red car, but that shouldn''t have been a problem since the photo that placed in front of me had a bunch of strawberrys with a lot of green on a reddish background (and even the winner has a lot of white on that lemon, but then white is not really a color right? :P). all in all, seeing the comments i realize that i may have messed with the contrast a bit too much but, in my opinion, the best way to outline a Ferrari is to present it on a dark background (and the challenge rules didn''t say anything about the luminosity of the background or that of the subject, just that they should be of the same color). And, it''s true, I oversharpend it just a bit to enhance the lines even more. i was expecting more comments on the photo itself than on the challenge requirements, anyway i placed a request for a review from the club, if they''ll ever get to my photo...', '2008-03-06 03:31:41.000000', '2008-03-06 16:08:06.000000', 0),
(4542560, 651610, 28742, '<td valign="top">Nice job, Sue! Feels like Spring! :)</td>', 'Nice job, Sue! Feels like Spring! :)', '2008-03-06 04:45:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542662, 650540, 39900, '<td valign="top">Totally awsome shot.. Con grats</td>', 'Totally awsome shot.. Con grats', '2008-03-06 07:36:31.000000', NULL, 0),
