(4543159, 650540, 89086, '<td valign="top">i''m not sure if he is serious but i agree with philup. such a lack of creativity</td>', 'i''m not sure if he is serious but i agree with philup. such a lack of creativity', '2008-03-06 11:33:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543254, 650571, 30982, '<td valign="top">I did vote this challenge and it''s too bad I''d seen this one ahead of time - definitely one of my favorites of what was a pretty darn good challenge!  Grats on yet another 6+!</td>', 'I did vote this challenge and it''s too bad I''d seen this one ahead of time - definitely one of my favorites of what was a pretty darn good challenge!  Grats on yet another 6+!', '2008-03-06 12:33:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543473, 650372, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is gorgeous - I love the color and the fade-to-blue in the upper right.  Excellent composition, very nice "feel" to the shot.</td>', 'This is gorgeous - I love the color and the fade-to-blue in the upper right.  Excellent composition, very nice "feel" to the shot.', '2008-03-06 14:12:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543485, 651658, 30982, '<td valign="top">Lovely quiet shot with wonderful blues.  Gotta say I don''t know where the bottle could be sharper - looks plenty sharp to me.</td>', 'Lovely quiet shot with wonderful blues.  Gotta say I don''t know where the bottle could be sharper - looks plenty sharp to me.', '2008-03-06 14:14:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543489, 651824, 30982, '<td valign="top">They make salt licks in cobalt blue?  Why?  Interesting contrast in textures and a great match in colors.</td>', 'They make salt licks in cobalt blue?  Why?  Interesting contrast in textures and a great match in colors.', '2008-03-06 14:16:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543492, 651673, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is very appealing and I think the beads added a lot to the composition and the feel - added an elegance if you will.  Very good, very rich color, too.  It''s easy to get green to be icky - here it''s wonderful.</td>', 'This is very appealing and I think the beads added a lot to the composition and the feel - added an elegance if you will.  Very good, very rich color, too.  It''s easy to get green to be icky - here it''s wonderful.', '2008-03-06 14:19:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543495, 651985, 30982, '<td valign="top">Awesome match on the reds and very strong diagonal composition.  How did you light this?</td>', 'Awesome match on the reds and very strong diagonal composition.  How did you light this?', '2008-03-06 14:21:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543500, 652057, 30982, '<td valign="top">Great job, Shez!  You have a very creative mind - you come up with the neatest ideas for these challenges, then you''re able to execute them well.  A very fun shot, this one!  And you set it out on a leaf, too, yes?  Very good idea for a background.</td>', 'Great job, Shez!  You have a very creative mind - you come up with the neatest ideas for these challenges, then you''re able to execute them well.  A very fun shot, this one!  And you set it out on a leaf, too, yes?  Very good idea for a background.', '2008-03-06 14:23:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543513, 651985, 11854, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> Awesome match on the reds and very strong diagonal composition.  How did you light this? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This was done in a light tent, lit from the top/behind with a halogen light. With the strong light through the fabric aimed directly at the bud it made it''s own vignette.</td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: Awesome match on the reds and very strong diagonal composition.  How did you light this?   This was done in a light tent, lit from the top/behind with a halogen light. With the strong light through the fabric aimed directly at the bud it made it''s own vignette.', '2008-03-06 14:29:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543526, 651673, 62318, '<td valign="top">You are too good at this thing. Beautiful rendition of green. A nice product placement shot with a twist.</td>', 'You are too good at this thing. Beautiful rendition of green. A nice product placement shot with a twist.', '2008-03-06 14:36:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543542, 650372, 62318, '<td valign="top">Wow Juli, wonderful purple/blue (mauve/cyan) color. Good framing and detail. The horizontal give a nice balance both on the petals and the stems. NIcely done.</td>', 'Wow Juli, wonderful purple/blue (mauve/cyan) color. Good framing and detail. The horizontal give a nice balance both on the petals and the stems. NIcely done.', '2008-03-06 14:45:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543776, 651131, 25166, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot and a splendid title. Great minds? Well done on another ribbon.</td>', 'Wonderful shot and a splendid title. Great minds? Well done on another ribbon.', '2008-03-06 16:50:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4544117, 651131, 75386, '<td valign="top">Great photo!<br/> <br/>He''s a veiled right? Nice looking guy! I had bugger I raised from 2 inches long.<br/> <br/>if you need any tips for care lemme know, cause, as Im sure you know, they can be a bit difficult</td>', 'Great photo! He''s a veiled right? Nice looking guy! I had bugger I raised from 2 inches long. if you need any tips for care lemme know, cause, as Im sure you know, they can be a bit difficult', '2008-03-06 20:37:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4544621, 650540, 49109, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Drake:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats on your win - this is a great shot. I read your comments with interest, about people "purposfully" voting low - on an obviously great picture. I had a couple of 1''s on my shot also (5th place Swans). Is this a regular thing?<br/>Drake </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Unfortunately yes. If you have a look at the top 5 of almost any challenge, you will notice that every shot  that looks like a typical dpc ribboning shot ( i.e. strong impact, tack sharp, well exposed, mass appealing subject) gets more 1s and 2s than shots that are not as easily recognizable as ribbon candidates, For some examples see the 4th in "Black and white", the 3rd, 4th and 5th in "Pet Portrait", 3rd, 4th and 5th in "Leading Lines", 2nd in "Peace" etc. So obviously there are some people that try to identify a future ribboner and vote it down by purpose.</td>', 'Originally posted by Drake: Congrats on your win - this is a great shot. I read your comments with interest, about people "purposfully" voting low - on an obviously great picture. I had a couple of 1''s on my shot also (5th place Swans). Is this a regular thing?Drake   Unfortunately yes. If you have a look at the top 5 of almost any challenge, you will notice that every shot  that looks like a typical dpc ribboning shot ( i.e. strong impact, tack sharp, well exposed, mass appealing subject) gets more 1s and 2s than shots that are not as easily recognizable as ribbon candidates, For some examples see the 4th in "Black and white", the 3rd, 4th and 5th in "Pet Portrait", 3rd, 4th and 5th in "Leading Lines", 2nd in "Peace" etc. So obviously there are some people that try to identify a future ribboner and vote it down by purpose.', '2008-03-07 03:15:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4544675, 650540, 34154, '<td valign="top">i dont think its identifying a potential winner and voting down on purpose, sometimes its just honest disinterest in the subject. this is technically a very well done photo, but i don''t check dpchallenge too often anymore and it seems like this shot is on the front page every few months now-</td>', 'i dont think its identifying a potential winner and voting down on purpose, sometimes its just honest disinterest in the subject. this is technically a very well done photo, but i don''t check dpchallenge too often anymore and it seems like this shot is on the front page every few months now-', '2008-03-07 04:23:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4544679, 650048, 82707, '<td valign="top">Purrrrfect!</td>', 'Purrrrfect!', '2008-03-07 04:45:18.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4544701, 650540, 49109, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by saloonstudios:</b></div><hr/><i> i dont think its identifying a potential winner and voting down on purpose, sometimes its just honest disinterest in the subject. this is technically a very well done photo, but i don''t check dpchallenge too often anymore and it seems like this shot is on the front page every few months now- </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Seriously, who would be so dumb to give out 1s just because a photo is not interesting for them? Those votes would be scrubbed at rollover, or do you really believe most of the other shots in the challenge would be far more interesting for such a person?<br/>Besides that, you could try and check last 200 challenges ribboners for a similar shot and look if you find more than one.  Even if you were right, it would only strengthen the theory that a specific kind of probable ribboners is easily identifiable.</td>', 'Originally posted by saloonstudios: i dont think its identifying a potential winner and voting down on purpose, sometimes its just honest disinterest in the subject. this is technically a very well done photo, but i don''t check dpchallenge too often anymore and it seems like this shot is on the front page every few months now-   Seriously, who would be so dumb to give out 1s just because a photo is not interesting for them? Those votes would be scrubbed at rollover, or do you really believe most of the other shots in the challenge would be far more interesting for such a person?Besides that, you could try and check last 200 challenges ribboners for a similar shot and look if you find more than one.  Even if you were right, it would only strengthen the theory that a specific kind of probable ribboners is easily identifiable.', '2008-03-07 05:36:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4545916, 650540, 61651, '<td valign="top">Very well-executed shot.  I need to use flash more in my shots - you show me what is possible.  This image is not an easy thing to accomplish -  congratulations on your blue ribbon!</td>', 'Very well-executed shot.  I need to use flash more in my shots - you show me what is possible.  This image is not an easy thing to accomplish -  congratulations on your blue ribbon!', '2008-03-07 14:48:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4545921, 651131, 61651, '<td valign="top">I really enjoy looking at this shot, I was one of your many 10s - I especially like the shallow DOF you chose.  Congratulations!</td>', 'I really enjoy looking at this shot, I was one of your many 10s - I especially like the shallow DOF you chose.  Congratulations!', '2008-03-07 14:52:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4545970, 651138, 45475, '<td valign="top">I think this image would have been better with a tighter crop and a straight down point of view. As it is, the ugly areas around the outside of the base(?) orange spoils the picture. Looks like you''ve used a vignette with a poor choice of blend mode, giving the image a rather dirty, flat look. I''ve found vignettes work remarkably well blended in either soft-light or over lay mode, but at a reduced opacity, say, 30-40%. Watch that focus too! Very important you have areas in focus that help the viewer through the image. At the moment, I''m stuck at mid-bottom with no desire to look further. <br/></td>', 'I think this image would have been better with a tighter crop and a straight down point of view. As it is, the ugly areas around the outside of the base(?) orange spoils the picture. Looks like you''ve used a vignette with a poor choice of blend mode, giving the image a rather dirty, flat look. I''ve found vignettes work remarkably well blended in either soft-light or over lay mode, but at a reduced opacity, say, 30-40%. Watch that focus too! Very important you have areas in focus that help the viewer through the image. At the moment, I''m stuck at mid-bottom with no desire to look further. ', '2008-03-07 15:17:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546043, 649510, 45475, '<td valign="top">I like the colour you chose and the hint of vignette. This garnered a 4 from me, which was quite generous considering the lack of focus. The comments below are a good indication that something was not right with this photograph. If the blur was intentional, it may have been wiser to exaggerate it. As it is now, it just looks like you couldn''t keep the camera steady :(</td>', 'I like the colour you chose and the hint of vignette. This garnered a 4 from me, which was quite generous considering the lack of focus. The comments below are a good indication that something was not right with this photograph. If the blur was intentional, it may have been wiser to exaggerate it. As it is now, it just looks like you couldn''t keep the camera steady :(', '2008-03-07 15:36:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546132, 651124, 45475, '<td valign="top">Blues are way to flat, dull. Maybe push the contrast or play with levels and curves adjustments in  your editing software? Compression has also degraded the image somewhat. When saving your image for dpc challenges, file size can be up to a maximum of 150kb, try to take advantage of that.</td>', 'Blues are way to flat, dull. Maybe push the contrast or play with levels and curves adjustments in  your editing software? Compression has also degraded the image somewhat. When saving your image for dpc challenges, file size can be up to a maximum of 150kb, try to take advantage of that.', '2008-03-07 16:02:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546425, 650571, 61651, '<td valign="top">Well-placed point of focus, and a handsome cat!  I like that the overall color scheme you chose for the challenge was not the norm.</td>', 'Well-placed point of focus, and a handsome cat!  I like that the overall color scheme you chose for the challenge was not the norm.', '2008-03-07 18:14:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546431, 650372, 61651, '<td valign="top">Wonderful pairing of foreground and background hues, Juli - you got good contrast out of very similar shade comparison.</td>', 'Wonderful pairing of foreground and background hues, Juli - you got good contrast out of very similar shade comparison.', '2008-03-07 18:15:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546436, 651658, 61651, '<td valign="top">Lovely - I like that offset bottle.</td>', 'Lovely - I like that offset bottle.', '2008-03-07 18:16:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546447, 651673, 61651, '<td valign="top">This is gorgeous - look at that commenters'' voting average!  I also like the complexity of this composition, with the three similarly-colored elements.</td>', 'This is gorgeous - look at that commenters'' voting average!  I also like the complexity of this composition, with the three similarly-colored elements.', '2008-03-07 18:20:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546453, 652057, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nicely put together, as always, Shez!  That is one humongous-looking pepper! ;)</td>', 'Nicely put together, as always, Shez!  That is one humongous-looking pepper! ;)', '2008-03-07 18:23:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547565, 649752, 87278, '<td valign="top">Red hot chilli! I like the ranking it got! Into my favs! Congrats!</td>', 'Red hot chilli! I like the ranking it got! Into my favs! Congrats!', '2008-03-08 05:49:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4547771, 650241, 26464, '<td valign="top">wow!<br/></td>', 'wow!', '2008-03-08 08:21:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4548083, 650540, 91168, '<td valign="top"><u><b>Wow.</b></u> <br/> <br/><i>Ive seen alot of this kind of pictures.  The ones that are in water. They are a little over-done, But this is a very good shot anyway.</i> <br/> <br/>Well done.<br/>From<br/>Lois.</td>', 'Wow.  Ive seen alot of this kind of pictures.  The ones that are in water. They are a little over-done, But this is a very good shot anyway.  Well done.FromLois.', '2008-03-08 11:23:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4548197, 651728, 91168, '<td valign="top"><b>Very imaginative. :)</b></td>', 'Very imaginative. :)', '2008-03-08 12:08:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4548362, 652061, 49380, '<td valign="top">OK, so I forgot when I was editing it that you can''t use layer masks on saturation :(, oh well, live and learn I guess. Oh, and thanks for all the great comments and critiques.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-08 13:24:32.</i></td>', 'OK, so I forgot when I was editing it that you can''t use layer masks on saturation :(, oh well, live and learn I guess. Oh, and thanks for all the great comments and critiques.', '2008-03-08 13:23:50.000000', '2008-03-08 13:24:32.000000', 0),
(4548416, 650371, 90495, '<td valign="top">I love insects and I love this type of photography. Nice timing by both of you.<br/>Technically this shot is flawless. I didn''t see this during voting, and I voted on over 50% of the entries, but it would''ve garnered a 9 for sure.<br/></td>', 'I love insects and I love this type of photography. Nice timing by both of you.Technically this shot is flawless. I didn''t see this during voting, and I voted on over 50% of the entries, but it would''ve garnered a 9 for sure.', '2008-03-08 13:51:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4548667, 651131, 26878, '<td valign="top">Way to go, all you need is a blue ribbon now.</td>', 'Way to go, all you need is a blue ribbon now.', '2008-03-08 16:41:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4548776, 650540, 34154, '<td valign="top">the 1 is uncalled for i agree with that, but 4''s and 5''s and to stretch it a 3 wouldn''t be unexpected though, and yes that would be for someone who had voted on every photo and still found this one less interesting than others. as far as a type of photo being identified as a ribboner during voting, yeah, i think a lot of times it IS obvious if the photo is good. but when its a photo that people have already seen ribbon in the past, it can change your opinion of it even if its flawless. MJ dunked from the free throw line and shocked the world. a lot of people can do that now but it doesn''t feel as shocking-<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by eyewave:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by saloonstudios:</b></div><hr/><i> i dont think its identifying a potential winner and voting down on purpose, sometimes its just honest disinterest in the subject. this is technically a very well done photo, but i don''t check dpchallenge too often anymore and it seems like this shot is on the front page every few months now- </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Seriously, who would be so dumb to give out 1s just because a photo is not interesting for them? Those votes would be scrubbed at rollover, or do you really believe most of the other shots in the challenge would be far more interesting for such a person?<br/>Besides that, you could try and check last 200 challenges ribboners for a similar shot and look if you find more than one.  Even if you were right, it would only strengthen the theory that a specific kind of probable ribboners is easily identifiable. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'the 1 is uncalled for i agree with that, but 4''s and 5''s and to stretch it a 3 wouldn''t be unexpected though, and yes that would be for someone who had voted on every photo and still found this one less interesting than others. as far as a type of photo being identified as a ribboner during voting, yeah, i think a lot of times it IS obvious if the photo is good. but when its a photo that people have already seen ribbon in the past, it can change your opinion of it even if its flawless. MJ dunked from the free throw line and shocked the world. a lot of people can do that now but it doesn''t feel as shocking- Originally posted by eyewave: Originally posted by saloonstudios: i dont think its identifying a potential winner and voting down on purpose, sometimes its just honest disinterest in the subject. this is technically a very well done photo, but i don''t check dpchallenge too often anymore and it seems like this shot is on the front page every few months now-   Seriously, who would be so dumb to give out 1s just because a photo is not interesting for them? Those votes would be scrubbed at rollover, or do you really believe most of the other shots in the challenge would be far more interesting for such a person?Besides that, you could try and check last 200 challenges ribboners for a similar shot and look if you find more than one.  Even if you were right, it would only strengthen the theory that a specific kind of probable ribboners is easily identifiable. ', '2008-03-08 17:26:02.000000', NULL, 0),
